Election:  General Election
Date: November 3, 2026
NOTICE OF GENERAL ELECTION
TUESDAY NOVEMBER 3, 2026
Mills County Auditor and Commissioner of Elections,
Amber Farnan
, hereby gives notice that there will be a GENERAL ELECTION in Mills County on
Tuesday November 3
, 20
26
Qualified electors of Mills County will vote at the polling places designated below for the purpose of
electing candidates for Federal, State, and County Offices.
Poll Hours
The Polls will open at
7:00 AM
and close at
8:00 PM
, as provided by law.
Voter Information
Voters are required to provide an approved form of photo ID at the polling place before receiving and casting a ballot. A voter who is unable to provide an approved form of ID (or proof residence if required) may:
Cast a provisional ballot and provide a photo ID / proof of residency at the Auditor’s Office by
8:30
AM
,
Friday
,
June 2
, 20
26
.
PLEASE NOTE:
With the passage of HF2501, the voter attestation process is no longer an option for pre-registered voters. However, voter attestation is still available for Election Day Registrants.
For additional information about providing proof of identity and/or residency visit:
https://voterready.iowa.gov/
or call (712) 527-3146.
Voter Registration Information
Voters must be registered to vote to participate in the City / School Election. Registration may be done in the following ways.
Voters may register in person in the Auditor’s Office. The deadline is
5:00 PM
,
Monday, October 19, 2026
.
Voters may mail in their registration to the Auditor’s Office. Voter registrations that are mailed must be received by or have been postmarked by
Monday, October 19, 2026
.
Election Day Registration: Voters may register at their polling place on Election Day by presenting a current photo ID and proof of residency to the election officials. Contact the Auditor’s Office for a list of approved documents.
Absentee Voting by Mail
A ballot may be mailed to voters upon their request. Requests can be made in writing (voters must include their name, ID #, address, date of birth, name and date of the election, voter signature, and signature date) or on an official Absentee Ballot Request form.
Official forms may be obtained by contacting the Auditor’s office or on our website at
https://www.millscountyiowa.gov/
.
Absentee Ballot
requests
must be received by the Auditor’s Office no later than
5:00
PM
on
Monday, October 19, 2026
.
Absentee
ballots
must be returned to the Auditor’s office no later than
8:00 PM
on
Tuesday, November 3, 2026
. Postmark dates
DO NOT
count. Absentee ballots
CANNOT
be placed in the drop box outside the Courthouse.
Voters may check the status of their absentee ballot by contacting the Mills County Auditor’s Office or at:
https://sos.iowa.gov/elections/absenteeballotstatus/absentee/search
Absentee Voting In-Person
Absentee ballots will be available starting
Wednesday, October 14, 2026
, at the Mills County Auditor’s Office and may be voted in the office until
4:30 PM
on
Monday, November 2, 2026
.
Public Test of Voting Equipment
Both the Unisyn Freedom Vote Scan voting system and ballot marking devices which will be use in the General Election will be tested starting at
10:00
AM
on
Thursday, October 22, 2026,
and will continue
Friday, October 23, 2026
, at
10:00 AM
, if necessary. The public test will be conducted at the Mills County Annex, in the basement at 403 Railroad Avenue Glenwood, IA 51534.
Provisional Ballot Board
The Provisional Ballot Board will meet at
8:30 AM
on
Friday, November 6, 2026
, in the boardroom at the Courthouse, to decide on any voter’s Provisional Ballot that was cast on Election Day.
Post-Election Audit
A hand count audit will be conducted of a voting precinct, randomly selected by the Iowa Secretary of State Office, at
9:30 AM
on
Friday, November 6, 2026
in the boardroom at the Courthouse. The purpose of the Post-Election Audit is to verify the results of the tabulating machine used in the election.
Designation of Polling Places
Please note the changes in polling places below for the Primary Election. Not all voters will be going to the same polling location that were used in the previous 2024 General Election. Polling places are handicap accessible. Any voter who is physically unable to enter the polling place has the right to vote in the voter’s vehicle. For further information, please contact the County Auditor’s Office. Voter can find their precinct and their polling place at the following link:
https://sos.iowa.gov/elections/voterreg/pollingplace/search.aspx
